Apple's <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-gb/121115">support document</a> does not explain whether its "up to 14GB" requirement is directly comparable with the Apple Intelligence "Storage" category in System Settings, or why some Macs display substantially higher numbers. (For what it's worth, we haven't seen the same ballooning figures on iPhones and iPads running iOS 27 and iPadOS 27.)<br/>
<br/>
It's not just academic, either. While using Apple Intelligence is optional, downloading its on-device models is not. Apple in macOS 27 and iOS 27 removed the toggle to disable Apple Intelligence, so users unequivocally have to set aside space for Apple's models. In an era where memory and storage costs are rising <em>because</em> of AI, the irony of this situation cannot be lost. It doesn't make it any less frustrating, though.<br/>
<br/>
